Article 12

In carrying out its obligations and responsibilities, the Regional Government has the authority to:

a. make policies and programs;
b. formulate implementation guidelines;
c. organize services;
d. coordinate policies, programs, budgets and services; e. conduct monitoring, supervision and evaluation of the implementation of prevention protection for victims of violence especially for women, children and their families.

Article 18

(1) Certain civil servant officials within the Regency Government are granted authority to conduct investigations into violations of the provisions in this Regional Regulation.

(2) The authority of investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) is: a. to receive reports or complaints from a person or family and other persons, regarding actions on violations of the Regional Regulation;

b. to conduct first actions and examinations at the scene; c. to bring in experts required in connection with the examination of the case;

d. to summon persons to be heard for their statements and examined as witnesses or suspects;

e. to take actions according to law that can be accounted for.

