c. enhance the institutional capacity of protection organizers, victims of violence especially for women, children and their families; d. establish a data and information center on protection, victims of violence especially for women, children and their families; e. conduct monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection, victims of violence especially for women, children and their families.

Article 1

In this Regional Regulation, the following terms are defined as:

1. Region means Blitar Regency;
2. Regional People's Representative Council of Blitar Regency, hereinafter abbreviated as DPRD, means the DPRD of Blitar Regency;
3. Regent means the Regent of Blitar;
4. Regional Government means the Government of Blitar Regency; 5. Community means individuals, families, groups and social organizations and/or community organizations;
6. Woman means a creature created by God with female sex, or with reproductive organs in the form of ovaries, ovum or egg cells, uterus, and hymen;
7. Child means a person who has not yet reached the age of 18 (eighteen) years, including a child still in the womb;
8. Protection of women and children means all efforts to protect women and children, starting from prevention, safeguarding and handling measures, aimed at providing a sense of security and comfort to women and children and their families, especially those who are victims of violence;
9. Victims of violence means women and children who experience violence and/or threats of violence whether physical, psychological, sexual or economic both in the domestic sphere and in the public sphere;
10. Violence means any act or omission of one's obligations that results in misery or suffering whether physical, mental, sexual and economic including threats to commit acts, coercion or unlawful deprivation of liberty;
11. Neglect means an act that results in a person's economic dependence on another person in one household; 12. Prevention means all efforts aimed at preventing the occurrence of violence and threats of violence;
13. Safeguarding means all efforts to ensure that women and children who are vulnerable to violence do not become victims of violence;
14. Handling means all efforts aimed at handling cases of violence against women and children and their families including litigation and non-litigation services;
15. Trafficking in persons means the act of recruitment, transportation, harboring, transfer, transfer, or receipt of a person by threat of violence, use of violence, abduction, confinement, forgery, fraud, abuse of power or vulnerable position, debt bondage or giving payment or benefits, so as to obtain consent from the person holding control over that other person, whether conducted within the country or between countries, for the purpose of exploitation or resulting in a person being exploited.
16. Sexual exploitation means any form of utilization of sexual organs or other body organs of the victim to gain profit, but is not limited to all activities of prostitution and indecency.
17. Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment (P2TP2A) means one form of service facility for women and children consisting of government and non-government elements in an effort to fulfill information and needs in the fields of education, health, economy, politics, law, fulfillment and prevention of acts of violence and trafficking against women and children.
18. Safe house means a temporary residence used to provide fulfillment for victims in accordance with established standard operating procedures.
19. Child in a normal or regular situation means a child who has the opportunity to grow and develop optimally.
20. Child as victim of violence means a child who becomes a victim of one or all types of violence, whether physical, psychological, sexual, or neglected by parents and family including victims of human trafficking;
21. Disabled child means a child with disabilities;
22. Parents means biological father and/or mother, or step father and/or mother, adoptive father and/or mother;
23. Family means the smallest unit in society consisting of husband and wife, or husband and wife and their children, or father and his children, or mother and her children, or blood relatives in direct ascending or descending line up to the third degree;
24. Guardian means a person or body who in fact exercises parental authority as a parent over a child;
25. Minimum Service Standard (SPM) means a performance benchmark for integrated service units in providing complaint handling services, health services, social rehabilitation, law enforcement and legal assistance as well as repatriation-social reintegration especially for women and children victims of violence
26. Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) means technical guidelines for the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence compiled based on Minimum Service Standards according to regional financial capacity.
27. Abandoned child means a child whose needs are not properly fulfilled by those obligated according to their capacity whether physical, mental and spiritual.
28. Related SKPD means SKPD which in its main tasks and functions handles the protection of women and children.
29. SKPD in charge of regional development planning means the Regional Development Planning Agency of Blitar Regency, hereinafter abbreviated as BAPEDA of Blitar Regency.
30. SKPD in charge of women's empowerment and child protection means the Women's Empowerment and Family Planning Agency of Blitar Regency.

Article 12

In carrying out its obligations and responsibilities, the Regional Government has the authority to:

a. make policies and programs;
b. formulate implementation guidelines;
c. organize services;
d. coordinate policies, programs, budgets and services; e. conduct monitoring, supervision and evaluation of the implementation of prevention protection for victims of violence especially for women, children and their families.

